Z||000013||BlackStang95||10-23-2001||11:38 PM||||I have realized now, that nothing I can say or do will ever get through to some of you, the bias and preconceived notions and assumptons just run too deep.  I don't know why some of you are too far gone, perhaps you are just stupid, or perhaps you've seen 16 year olds in Mustangs beat you too many times, I dont know.  I will do my best to ignore this type of forum user in the future.  Consider this message for the rest of you guys:<P>I don't own a fiero, I've never owned a car other than my black 1994 Mustang V-6.  I had always loved Mustangs, ever since childhood, but I never thought i'd be able to afford one on my Mcdonalds salary.   I bought my car in december of 98 it had 120,000 miles on it and it was clear it had a very rough life.  The inside was full of cigarette butts and ashes, the engine had been previously blown and it was then replaced with one from a 95.  It also had the broken differential.  I paid $3500 cash for it, and I was happy cuz I'd finally gotten the car of my dreams.  I spent at least 20 hours just cleaning the inside of the car, I scrubbed and shampooed every bit of carpet, I washed and armor alled every piece of trim, washed and waxed the outside 3 times.  I replaced the serpentine belt, the wiper blades, the spark plugs and wires, the air filter, changed the oil, changed the coolant, and replaced the driver seatbelt.  I replaced the shocks and struts and put new tires on.  I don't regret any of it.  I love my car, it's perfect for me and I wouldn't trade it for anything but a faster Mustang.  <P>Why am i here?  I like talking about cars, its all me and my friends do.  My best friend of 8 years just bought a fiero gt after wanting one for years.  I've spent many hours helping him work on it and riding with him in it.  I like the ride, the looks, and the sound.  I don't think I'd like it for me as a daily driver because of the non power steering and the 2 seater part.  <P>I don't believe car people need to be narrow minded or in "teams" based on what they drive.  The only kinds of cars I hate are rice and suvs.  They are the enemy.  Everything else is 2 sides of the same coin.   <P>I didn't come here and trash talk fieros, I defened my car against people who insulted my car, having seen nothing but my user name.<P>Too many fieros, If you really had a question for me, you should have private messaged...its obvious to me you asked here cuz you wanted all your buddies to have your back.  Well, mission accomplished.||||reg||1
Z||000014||California Kid||10-24-2001||12:01 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||10-24-2001||12:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>its obvious to me you asked here cuz you wanted all your buddies to have your back.  Well, mission accomplished.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nah, I wouldn't worry about that too much. I've followed along with moderate interest and I've seen PFF regs go way over the line in slamming you and your choice of ride. Personally, I think the whole mess about "what's faster" is a totally moot point. Far too many other variables come into play, and besides, who gives a rats a-hole? There is ALWAYS someone faster. Yawn. I think it's very commendable that a young guy has the initiative to save up $3500 of McPaychecks instead of blowing it on dope to buy the car he has long lusted over. I say right effin on! I think anyone on this forum who has a soul can identify with the hours out in the driveway cleaning, polishing and waxing, replacing little crap that wears out, whatever. Just because you don't lockstep to the beat of "our" band doesn't make your intelligence suspect. <P>Anyhow, at this point, I can say that you have won an ally in the ol stimp, and God help those who wanna keep flogging this dead stanky horse.<P>Peace kid.||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||10-24-2001||12:17 AM||||I'm glad I stayed out of this one till now. <P>Stang, you keep posts like this coming, and I'll have no problems with you. <P>It's the lying and BS numbers (and the ignorance) that gets to me. <BR>You can stop lying, and as for ignorance, you'll learn more in time. Just sit back, enjoy the cars, and learn. You'll have no problems that way...<P>Later days!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Pontiaddict||10-24-2001||12:38 AM||||I don't buy it. <BR>Most of my friends are Ford fans and I don't have a problem with Fords. I tried to stay out of the Camaro and MR2 flame fests because I kept an open mind about different cars being cool in their own way. I don't even have anything against imports, although I do laugh at the ones being posers.<P>But you're just a punk. Your first post was slamming Fieros and you seem to think that everyone who doesn't like you, hates you becasue of the type of car you drive. [That's kind of narrow minded don't you think?] Face it, if you were driving a McLaren F-1 you'd still be a worthless punk kid. And there would still be people here that would laugh at you for owning one, just to laugh at <B>you</B>. You'll get no respect from me, because you show none to anyone else here. You'll get no pity from me with your little sob story either.<P>If you don't like it, too bad.||||reg||1
