Z||000024||Mach10||10-24-2001||02:46 AM||||I said that I would stand down, and I so I will say only this: I looked over the entirety of Stang's threads, only to find that there were a lot of legitimate ones made. He's only ever gotten in a few fights (albeight large ones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) in his stay here. Some of his stuff has shown him to be immature, but the majority of the posts he's made, OUTSIDE of the flamewars have been no better or worse than the rest of the people here. <P>Blackstang: You don't have to defend your car ruthlessly everytime someone makes a crack at the same make/model. When someone makes fun of my car, I laugh and drive on. I'd suggest some of the same? As funny as flame wars can be (and I've considered ours to be a source of much entertainment on long shifts at work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), they can and do become tiresome, and tend to strain relationships, even virtual ones like these.<BR>NOW, Since you are still here, there must be something that you want from us. There's no reason in the world why you cannot use us as a resource like everyone else does. If that's not your aim, and your aim is to fight tooth and nail about your car, I can say with certainty that you will not be welcome. But I don't think that's the case. 90% of your posts are legitimate and constructive. It's the glaring 10% that speak loudest. So how's it going to be? Are we all gonna continue to fight until Cliff steps in and does something extreme, or are we ALL going to simmer down, relax, and continue with business as usual? <P>The choice is yours. The community here has shown to have a short memory for stuff like this. You don't have to be on the defensive all the time. Choose.<P>Sean||||reg||6
