Z||000028||ur2biteme||10-24-2001||05:59 AM||||i dont know what this has to do with the whole thing, but i'm gonna put my $.02 in:<P>i owned a '94 mustang with an auto for a year back in 97-98.  great car, wasnt that sluggish in my opinion (just under 8 seconds to 60 on a downhill onramp isnt a race car either).  it was also in extremely good condition as well, as it should have been with just under 40k miles on it.  not a single problem, and my mom only had minor problems (mainly caused by slight neglect and a moderate front end accident) when she had it from between 65k to 130k.  suprising handling for a straight axle.  fun car.<P>my fiero i purchased because i couldnt afford the $330 payments anymore.  paid $1600 for it, and i paid too much.  it was bleeding from every possible location it seemed, but i got from 117k to 175k with it, and it dealt well with my harsh driving habits considering it's allready bad condition.  it was a dog, but it was a 4.  i've still got the car and i'm planning on building up a 3.1 for it at the junior college this spring.  braking could be better, but it's quick, light (contrary to some people's opinions), and quite the nimble handler.  very few fieros are straight line monsters and i can accept that.  <P>next comes my Z.  the best $2500 i've ever spent.  an EXTREMELY well kept daily driver with 210k miles, but runs and handles like it's got 40k.  even with the auto it's gotta be the hardest launching car i've owned, and the braking is far better than the previous mentioned and the handling is almost on par with my fiero (Z's got body roll, fiero dont  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  plus, unlike my pounded fiero, all the options work (the a/c was nice this summer) but i do recall that my friend, the previous owner, mentioned he got burned by some punk kid in his mommy's bonneville ssei.  i have to agree there is always someone faster......<P>anyway, the point(s) i'm trying to make is that the cars are different, and there is some prejudice over what car is better.  however, this is the FIERO fourm.  i'm sure blackstang you probably get sick of some camaro guys giving you crap for not complying with their status quo, as i know i got ALOT of crap about my fiero being a fire trap and such with all the problems i had with it, but i like it, and i want to build it and drive it with the respect it deserves.  i seem to remember that we had some MR2 board guys here that stirred up trouble, as i can also remember we had some here that were cool, and interested, and i think at least one owned a fiero as well.  i'm just saying that regardless of what kind of car you drive (this isnt entirely directed to you blackstang), if you come on the board to get some info, or even want to make some general comparisons, or just chat about our cars civily, most people here probably would be willing to help.  but when it's turned into a giant pissing contest there are those involved that are gonna be looking to burn ya at the stake.  <P>in other words, i ain't got no problems wit'cha, just keep it cool dog, aight?  <P>take it easy guys||||reg||1
Z||000029||Cliff Pennock||10-24-2001||06:21 AM||||I'm surprised. I would've expected this thread to be and orgy of four-letter words and by now I would be busy filling up the ban-list with ip-addresses, usernames and email-addresses. Instead, I find <B>this</B>.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Let me just add my 2c: The <B>only</B> reason I have warned blackstang twice now, is because of his use of (foul) language and the fact he has said some stupid things like "most cops deserve to be shot" or his remarks about using "butterfly-knives" if ever he meets certain forum members. <B>Not</B> because he drives a Mustang, <B>not</B> because he vigorously defends his ride - but merely for the earlier mentioned reasons. In fact, I <B>have</B> seen all his legit posts, where he actually contributes to a discussion. And his post above shows he <B>can</B> keep it civilized. He's still on strike two however. One more strike and he's out.<P>Blackstang, this is a <B>Fiero</B> forum. That means that most people here will defend their ride just as vigorously as you do. With one exception: you are completely outnumbered. So let them bash the Mustang all they want, it's what we do here: pretending our cars are the best thing since sliced bread and everything else is "just a car". The Fiero is the better car. On the other hand, if I owned a Mustang, then a Mustang would be the better car. If this was a Yugo forum, a Yugo would be the best car ever built. Get my point? You don't walk into the IBM building trying to convince the employees there that a Dell is a much better computer. Because no matter what the truth is, chances are you'll get thrown out in no time.<P>So there's absolutely no need to go defend your car whenever somebody trashes it here. You will never find much support - regardless of the BS content the original trashing had.<P>The reason why you are not liked here (understatement) by so many people, is <B>not</B> because you drive a Mustang, but because you disturb our little fictional Eden where the Fiero <B>is</B> the best car ever built.<P>Understand that, and you're welcome to stay.||||reg||1
Z||000030||tomanyfieros||10-24-2001||07:30 AM||||black. i did not post this here because i wanted back up. i wanted to post it here because i have picked these ?'s out that i have read and some people have asked about this and no reply about it because the post was colsed. me, i would not need back up, if i started to get into a fight, i would back down, just becaus it is in my best interest to keep the fights down, as well as keeping cliff from colsing posts... i only wanted me, and everyone on this thread to see, we can all get along. look, u got people on ur side because of this post now. they know where u come from. a person who is  into there car as we are, just a different car. i know how it was working, well, not as long as u. i worked to get about 200 so i could buy the car. (84 coupe).... anyways, i will be (if it is not closed) posting my tonite, i have to go, or the bus will miss me. <BR>stang, i am not against u, there is some stangs i like. i think that if u were to claim down, relax, and drink what ever u want. we would start to ome back and maybe (maybe) like you. <BR>got to go, see u all later!<BR>thanx cliff for not closing this post!<BR>Jason||||reg||1
